{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083352-wait-13-6th-rank-garou-were-sacrificed-to-stop-the-stormeater","id":1083352,"title":"Wait 13 6th rank Garou were Sacrificed to stop the Stormeater?!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-24T22:54:13-07:00","id":1083352,"title":"Wait 13 6th rank Garou were Sacrificed to stop the Stormeater?!","content":"That seems really excessive since the books mention each tribe might not even have a 6th rank at any given time. I'm not really convinced 13 would be gathered to kill themselves. I know the Stormeater was approaching Celestine status!<br /> <br /> 13 6th rank together means a world wide Garou Unity, and this isn't reflected in the setting. 13 6th ranks can do impossible things, and they never got together to do things like save the silent striders or stargazers but they saved Amaerica?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T01:19:46-07:00","id":1083379,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you want anyone to say.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a bit of an insane idea. You have two choices: accept that it happened that way and the Garou got lucky that each Tribe had a Legendary Ranked individual around that was willing to join in the effort with all the implications that entails, or treat it as a story that might not be 100% true (maybe they were mostly just experienced Elders that were bumped up to Legendary after their sacrifices, maybe it was 13 but not actually one from each Tribe, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T05:36:26-07:00","id":1083415,"title":"","content":"Behold the glories of their Sterling editorial Acumen!!<br /> <br /> I remember in Exalted Savage Sea's &quot;An unexalted Captain is almost unheard of&quot;<br /> <br /> This puts almost half the scarlet dynasty captaining ships...<br /> <br /> Not to mention Dragon blooded holding other officer positions...<br /> <br /> This seems to have been (for once) rightfully retconned, which Im very glad of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-25-2017, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T05:55:30-07:00","id":1083419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083352-wait-13-6th-rank-garou-were-sacrificed-to-stop-the-stormeater?p=1083379#post1083379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you want anyone to say.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a bit of an insane idea. You have two choices: accept that it happened that way and the Garou got lucky that each Tribe had a Legendary Ranked individual around that was willing to join in the effort with all the implications that entails, or treat it as a story that might not be 100% true (maybe they were mostly just experienced Elders that were bumped up to Legendary after their sacrifices, maybe it was 13 but not actually one from each Tribe, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume it was posthumous promotion to Rank 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"k